1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,564
This is Flotilla, a read-only dashboard that shows a user's Google Analytics 4 properties on one screen.

2
00:00:06,564 --> 00:00:11,739
The signed-in user clicks Sign in with Google to connect their Analytics account.

3
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:14,800
This starts Google's OAuth flow.

4
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,489
The address bar shows Flotilla's OAuth client ID.

5
00:00:18,489 --> 00:00:22,030
The user chooses the Google account to connect.

6
00:00:22,729 --> 00:00:28,668
Flotilla is pending verification, so Google shows the unverified app screen.

7
00:00:28,668 --> 00:00:33,199
The user selects Advanced, then continues to Flotilla HQ.

8
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:39,086
First, Sign in with Google uses the open ID, email, and profile scopes.

9
00:00:39,086 --> 00:00:45,150
Flotilla uses these only to identify the user and show which account is connected.

10
00:00:45,849 --> 00:00:50,111
Next, Flotilla requests the sensitive scope, analytics.

11
00:00:50,111 --> 00:00:55,458
readonly, shown here as: See and download your Google Analytics data.

12
00:00:55,458 --> 00:00:59,875
This is the only Analytics permission Flotilla asks for.

13
00:00:59,875 --> 00:01:02,509
The user grants it and continues.

14
00:01:03,209 --> 00:01:12,888
Flotilla uses this scope to list the GA4 properties the user can access, and to run read-only reports with the Google Analytics Data API.

15
00:01:12,888 --> 00:01:20,164
That includes live visitors, users, sessions, page views, engagement, top pages, and traffic channels.

16
00:01:20,164 --> 00:01:23,767
This data is only displayed to the signed-in user.

17
00:01:23,767 --> 00:01:29,560
Flotilla never modifies Analytics settings or data, and never sells or shares it.

18
00:01:30,259 --> 00:01:32,272
Users can sign out at any time.

19
00:01:32,272 --> 00:01:40,389
The Disconnect button revokes Google access and deletes the stored tokens, and Delete account erases all of the user's data.

20
00:01:40,389 --> 00:01:44,869
Access can also be revoked from the Google Account permissions page.
